- **Tune the TTL from observed reuse and freshness needs.** Your current **1,200-second** TTL can be a reasonable starting point for stable translations; measure hit rate and memory use before changing it.
- **Batch when translating multiple texts together.** DeepL accepts multiple texts in one request, which can reduce network overhead. Use this only when the caller has several texts ready; don’t delay a single chat message just to form a batch.
- **Limit concurrency** to protect your service and respect provider limits. Parallelize independent translations, but avoid unbounded `Promise.all` on large input sets.
- **Use retries sparingly.** Retry rate limits and transient server errors with backoff (and honor `Retry-After` when present); don’t retry validation or authentication failures. Set an overall timeout so retries cannot hold a chat request open indefinitely.
